(target: both agents)
This diff contains shell scripts. Trace quoting boundaries
through adjacent tokens — `"prefix"$var"suffix"` concatenates
safely, but `$var"text"` leaves var unquoted. Verify `set -euo
pipefail` is present at the top of scripts. Check `||` vs `&&`
chains — `cmd1 && cmd2 || cmd3` does NOT mean "if cmd1 and cmd2
succeed, else cmd3" because cmd3 runs if cmd2 fails even when
cmd1 succeeded. Verify variables used in arithmetic or array
indexing are validated. Check for unquoted `$@` in function
arguments. When a loop removes `break`, check if the new
behavior silently overwrites files from earlier iterations.
Verify `set -f` / `set +f` glob protection is consistent across
similar loops in the same file. When `export` is removed from
variable assignments, verify child processes (subprocess calls,
sourced scripts) can still see the variable.
